---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import profile from '../../data/profile.json';
const updated = 'November 18, 2026';
---
<Layout lang="en" title="Privacy policy" description="How Eduardo León Hernández handles the personal data received through this site, under Costa Rica's Law 8968." alternate="/privacidad/">
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    <div class="notice"><p><strong>Template pending review.</strong> This text follows Costa Rica's Law 8968 on the Protection of Individuals with Regard to the Processing of their Personal Data and its regulations, but it is not legal advice and should be reviewed by a qualified lawyer before being treated as final. The Spanish version prevails.</p></div>

    <h2>Controller</h2>
    <p>{profile.name}, an individual based in San José, Costa Rica, is responsible for the data received through this site. For any privacy question, use the <a href="/en/#contacto">contact form</a> or reach out on LinkedIn.</p>

    <h2>What data is collected and why</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Contact form:</strong> your name, email address and the message you write. They are used only to answer your request or prepare a quote. They are not used for advertising and are never sold or shared with third parties.</li>
      <li><strong>WhatsApp and LinkedIn:</strong> if you choose those channels, you leave this site and the conversation is also governed by Meta's (WhatsApp) or LinkedIn's policies.</li>
      <li><strong>Browsing:</strong> this site uses no cookies, analytics, tracking pixels or embedded third-party content. Fonts are served from this same site.</li>
      <li><strong>Theme preference:</strong> if you switch between light and dark mode, your browser stores that choice in its local storage (<code>localStorage</code>). It never leaves your device and you can clear it from your browser settings.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Legal basis</h2>
    <p>Processing is based on your informed consent, given when you submit the form after reading this policy (article 5 of Law 8968). You can withdraw it at any time.</p>

    <h2>Service providers involved</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Web3Forms</strong> receives the form data and forwards it to my email. It may process it outside Costa Rica.</li>
      <li><strong>GitHub Pages</strong> (GitHub, Inc.) hosts the site. Like any web server, it may log your IP address and technical visit data for security and operations, under its own privacy statement.</li>
      <li><strong>Email provider</strong> where messages are received and stored.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>By using these services, your data may be transferred to and stored outside Costa Rica.</p>

    <h2>How long data is kept</h2>
    <p>Messages are kept for as long as the conversation lasts and up to 12 months after the last contact, unless an ongoing business relationship requires keeping them longer. They are deleted afterwards.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>You can exercise your rights of access, rectification and erasure of your data at any time, and withdraw your consent. Send your request through the contact form stating what you need; you will receive an answer within the legal deadlines. If you believe your rights were not respected, you can contact Costa Rica's data protection agency (PRODHAB).</p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>The site is served only over HTTPS, applies a Content Security Policy (CSP) that limits which resources can load and includes no third-party scripts. If you find a security issue, see the <a href="/.well-known/security.txt">security.txt</a> file.</p>

    <h2>Minors</h2>
    <p>This site is aimed at adults and businesses. Data from minors is not knowingly collected.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes, the date above will be updated.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
